2. Bind physical keys to keyboard bar when it has focus
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/keyboard-bar.js': Listen for keydown on self when focused, intercept bound keys, stop propagation
        - In onConnect: set this.tabIndex = 0 (makes the custom element focusable)
        - In onConnect: attach a keydown listener on `this`:
            - If event.ctrlKey || event.altKey || event.metaKey → return (let it bubble to global handler)
            - Define a set of bound keys: the union of sharedDomKeys, pudDomKeys, promptKeys
            - If event.key is not in that set → return (let it bubble)
            - Look up the button: this.querySelector(`.kb-btn[data-key="${event.key}"]`)
            - If button found: event.stopPropagation(); event.preventDefault(); call this.#onButtonClick(btn)
            - If button not found: return (shouldn't happen, but let it bubble)
        - No changes to #onButtonClick itself; it already handles the fetch, state repaint, and prompt-ready dispatch
    [x] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Focus the keyboard bar element when showing it
        - In #showKeyboardBar(): after this.#keyboardBar.classList.remove('hidden'), add this.#keyboardBar.focus()
        - No other changes needed; global handler remains untouched and simply won't receive events the kb bar consumed
